message: "If you use or discuss this framework, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "The Saka Law: Measuring Recursive Technological Acceleration and Its Implications for Biomedical Longevity"
version: "0.3.2"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
authors:
  - family-names: "Carrasco"
    given-names: "Javier"
    alias: "Saka"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CarrascoOlmedoDevs/saka-law"
abstract: >-
  A falsifiable forecasting hypothesis and measurement framework for recursive
  technological acceleration: when technology materially improves the process by
  which new technology is discovered, validated and deployed, the growth rate of
  technological progress can itself increase. The framework operationalizes this
  across AI, compute, energy, laboratory automation, biotechnology, data, space,
  manufacturing and clinical translation, with dated quantitative predictions and
  a preregistered calibration protocol. Conceptual paper, not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - technological forecasting
  - recursive acceleration
  - research productivity
  - idea production function
  - artificial intelligence
  - longevity escape velocity
  - preregistration
